# GREYZONE brand

Source: `GREYZONE_Brand_Guidelines.pdf`. Do not invent colors, type roles, or claims.

Use only these colors: white `#FFFFFF`, black `#0A0A0A`, signal `#D1162C`, deep `#9E0F20`, grey `#868A90`, mist `#E4E5E7`, paper `#F4F4F2`, ink `#55585D`, graphite `#1C1D1F`. Tokens live in `app/globals.css`.

- White is the default page. Paper is for panels. Black and graphite are for dark surfaces.
- One signal-red action per view. Deep red is hover and pressed only.
- Red text only on white, at 16px or larger. Button labels are white on signal red.
- Black on white, white on black. Ink is secondary text on light. Grey is secondary on dark.
- Mist is the light divider. Graphite is the dark divider. No decorative borders or shadows.

Type roles already in the theme: `text-h1` 64/72, `text-h2` 40/48, `text-h3` 28/36, `text-subtitle` 18/26, `text-body` 16/26, `text-caption` 12/18, `text-button` 14/20, `text-label` 11/16. Use at most a headline, a subtitle, and body in one view.

Proxima Nova and Glitz are not in the repo. Keep the system sans stack. Do not load a lookalike font. Do not draw or retype the logo. Use the words GREYZONE as plain text until the supplied logo files are added.

Say it plainly. No jargon, no unsupported claims.
